# oracle: compute body/local (id 1 2 3) on four 2d nparticle bodies (cut down from examples/body data.body, 6/4/3/5 sub-particles), fix nve/body with pair body/nparticle and enforce2d, 200 steps; the compute's local array (id, x, y, z of every sub-particle, rows in atom order) is written by dump local at step 0 and step 200 and compared token by token; thermo pe ke etotal and the final atom state
# Measured max relative error: 5e-9 for the local array (native dump local prints 8 significant digits whatever dump_modify says, and every printed value matches the engine exactly; the file check is filerel=1e-14 with abs 1e-12) and 1e-9 for thermo and the final atom state (rel 1e-9, the case tolerance; the measured value is below it).
# oracle-inputs: w152body_local_nparticle.data
# oracle-files: w152body_local_nparticle.dump
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-9 abs=1e-12 filerel=1e-14
units           lj
dimension       2
atom_style      body nparticle 2 6
atom_modify     sort 0 0.0
read_data       w152body_local_nparticle.data
velocity        all create 1.44 87287 loop geom
pair_style      body/nparticle 5.0
pair_coeff      * * 1.0 1.0
neighbor        0.5 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
fix             1 all nve/body
fix             2 all enforce2d
compute         1 all body/local id 1 2 3
dump            1 all local 200 w152body_local_nparticle.dump index c_1[1] c_1[2] c_1[3] c_1[4]
thermo_style    custom step pe ke etotal
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          200
run             200
